{"name":"Shovel Knight","hex":"#37c4fa","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shovel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hand tool with a handle, used for moving portions of material such as earth, snow, and grain from one place to another, with some forms also used for digging. In strict usage differentiated from a spade, which is designed solely for small-scale digging and incidental tasks such as chopping of small roots.","A mechanical part of an excavator with a similar function."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move materials with a shovel.","To move with a shoveling motion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shovel"},{"term":"knight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young servant or follower; a trained military attendant in service of a lord.","A minor nobleman with an honourable military rank who had served as a page and squire."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To confer knighthood upon.","To promote (a pawn) to a knight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shovel Knight","blocks":[{"text":"Shovel Knight is a platform game developed and published by Yacht Club Games. Development was crowdfunded and the game was released for Nintendo 3DS, Wii U, and Windows in June 2014. It was ported to OS X and Linux in September 2014, PlayStation 3, PlayStation 4, PlayStation Vita, and Xbox One in April 2015, Amazon Fire TV in September 2015, and Nintendo Switch in March 2017. Shovel Knight is inspired by gameplay and graphics of platformer games developed for the Nintendo Entertainment System."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c8/Shovel_knight_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shovel_Knight","wikidata":"Q13427374"},{"title":"Shovel","blocks":[{"text":"A shovel is a tool used for digging, lifting, and moving bulk materials, such as soil, coal, gravel, snow, sand, or ore. Most shovels are hand tools consisting of a broad blade fixed to a medium-length handle. Shovel blades are usually made of sheet steel or hard plastics and are very strong. Shovel handles are usually made of wood or glass-reinforced plastic (fiberglass)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Skovl.jpg/330px-Skovl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shovel","wikidata":"Q7220961"},{"title":"Knight","blocks":[{"text":"A knight is a person granted an honorary title of a knighthood by a head of state or representative for service to the monarch, the church, or the country, especially in a military capacity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Codex_Manesse_Hartmann_von_Aue.jpg/330px-Codex_Manesse_Hartmann_von_Aue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knight","wikidata":"Q102083"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f0/Shovel_Knight_screenshot.png/330px-Shovel_Knight_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f0/Shovel_Knight_screenshot.png/330px-Shovel_Knight_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pre-release screenshot depicting Shovel Knight digging through dirt blocks","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShovel_Knight_screenshot.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/PAX_East_March_28_2026_Sean_Velasco_Yacht_Club_panel_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-PAX_East_March_28_2026_Sean_Velasco_Yacht_Club_panel_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/PAX_East_March_28_2026_Sean_Velasco_Yacht_Club_panel_%28cropped%